From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:26:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fun.py: a node follows the launches of a hashfun site and
 mines their QWEN curve

hashfun (https://github.com/staccDOTsol/hashfun) issues each coin on a chain
of its own along two curves; a block on the QWEN curve owes qwen on this
chain, proven inside the coin's chain against a relay of this chain's
headers. tools/fun.py is what a node does with that, and nothing of it runs
unless the folder names a site (HASHFUN) and a release (HASHFUNPKG, by
sha256): the package fetched and checked, the site's launches taken on with
their Qwencoin anchor checked against this node, a wallet fun whose keys
each launch's node holds, qwen moved into it through ord's wallet within
MIND_STEP and FUN_LIMIT (else MIND_LIMIT), a pool per launch on its QWEN
curve and a share of one core to mine with. A node that cannot dial the
site's node of a launch reaches it through the site's pages. A follower
reads Bitcoin only from a source its owner names (FUN_BTC); the file FUNBTC
is the site's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
